    "examples": [
      {
        "question_text": "Find each final amount, to the nearest cent.\n(a) Increase $\\$276$ by $13\\%$, then increase the result by $7\\%$.\n(b) Decrease $\\$148$ by $17\\%$, then decrease the result by $9\\%$.",
        "solution_text": "(a) Multipliers: $1.13$ and $1.07$.\n$1.13\\times1.07=1.2091$.\n$276\\times1.2091\\approx\\$333.71$.\n(b) Multipliers: $0.83$ and $0.91$.\n$0.83\\times0.91=0.7553$.\n$148\\times0.7553\\approx\\$111.78$.\nEach second change applies to the amount after the first change."
      },
      {
        "question_text": "A price increases by $18\\%$, then the new price decreases by $11\\%$. Find the single multiplier and the overall percentage change.",
        "solution_text": "Multipliers: $1.18$ and $0.89$.\n$1.18\\times0.89=1.0502$.\nThe new price is $105.02\\%$ of the original.\n$105.02\\%-100\\%=5.02\\%$: an overall increase."
      },
      {
        "question_text": "A positive quantity increases by $24\\%$, then decreases by $24\\%$.\n(a) Find the overall percentage change and explain why the two changes do not cancel.\n(b) Show whether reversing the order changes the final result.",
        "solution_text": "(a) $1.24\\times0.76=0.9424$.\nThe final quantity is $94.24\\%$ of the original.\n$100\\%-94.24\\%=5.76\\%$: a decrease.\nThe decrease is taken from the larger amount after the increase, not from the original.\n(b) $0.76\\times1.24=0.9424$ also.\nMultiplying these same two factors in either order gives the same final quantity."
      },
      {
        "question_text": "(a) A swimmer swims $0.8$ km on day 1 and increases the distance each day by $\\dfrac25$ of the previous day's distance. Find the distance on day 6, to the nearest $100$ metres.\n(b) Write the single multiplier for decreasing an amount by $8\\%$ each year for $9$ years.",
        "solution_text": "(a) Daily multiplier $=1+\\dfrac25=1.4$.\nFrom day 1 to day 6 there are $5$ increases.\n$0.8\\times1.4^5=4.302592\\text{ km}$.\nTo the nearest $100$ metres, the distance is $4.3$ km.\n(b) One year leaves $100\\%-8\\%=92\\%$, or $0.92$.\nNine successive decreases use $0.92^9$."
      }
    ],
